% F46-SEARCH: DEFECT 46.  SEARCH_STRING OF A SOURCE OF FFFF BYTES OR MORE
% SEARCHED GROUPS THAT EACH LEFT OUT PATLEN-1 BYTES, SO A PATTERN AT THE
% END OF THE SOURCE WAS NOT FOUND, AND WHEN THE GROUPS CAME OUT EVEN IT
% BEGAN PATLEN-1 BYTES BEFORE THE SOURCE.  THE TEST ONLY READS: THE SHIPPED
% CODE REGION HAS NO ROOM FOR 64 KB OF SCRATCH.  CASE 1 LOOKS FOR THE 200
% CODE BYTES AT THE END OF 65536 BYTES (512 BELOW CODE_PNTR, PAST ITS PAGE
% PADDING); CASE 2 FOR THE 200 DICTIONARY BYTES THAT START 199 BEFORE A
% SOURCE OF 2 X (FFFF-199) AT FC00.  EACH LINE PRINTS THE FLAG AND THE REST
% OF THE SOURCE (LENGTH, OFFSET).  PATCHED: -1 0 65536, THEN 0.
DECIMAL
CODE_PNTR @ 66048 - 'SB CONSTANT
SB 65336 + 200 SB 65536 SEARCH_STRING = = SB - = 2DROP CR
64512 199 - 200 64512 130672 SEARCH_STRING = = 64512 - = 2DROP CR
12345 = CR
